pokeplatinum-route5.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum): the route pilot answers the post-battle evolution's
"should a move be deleted?" question No. evolution.c Evolution_Main (every frame of the evolution task, which battle_main.c runs after a
battle that evolves a Pokemon) calls PortRoute4_EvoMenu (port/game/route_gen4.c) with whether the state is PRINT_SHOULD_A_MOVE_BE_DELETED ..
PROCESS_INPUT_SHOULD_A_MOVE_BE_DELETED; the pilot then presses B (gPortRouteYesNo 2) instead of A, whose default Yes opens the summary screen's
move pick where the leg stalled. No game behaviour changes; the DS build never sees the patch.
Handover-ID: none (port-only)

diff --git a/src/evolution.c b/src/evolution.c
--- a/src/evolution.c
+++ b/src/evolution.c
@@ -253,6 +253,10 @@ enum EvolutionState {
 };
 
+void PortRoute4_EvoMenu(int noQuestion); // the port's route pilot (port/game/route_gen4.c)
+
 static void Evolution_Main(EvolutionData *evolutionData)
 {
+    PortRoute4_EvoMenu(evolutionData->state >= EVOLUTION_STATE_PRINT_SHOULD_A_MOVE_BE_DELETED
+                       && evolutionData->state <= EVOLUTION_STATE_PROCESS_INPUT_SHOULD_A_MOVE_BE_DELETED);
     if (evolutionData->shrinkAndGrowState) {
         if ((evolutionData->shrinkAndGrowState & 1) == 0) {
